{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793028162,"nonce":"YYBEYi5gLGKWXxMIxWiDS/hk/u8=","title":"Bound native and hosted workspace connection admission","message":"Session documents are bounded, but a workspace can still allocate an unlimited number of socket connections. Add atomic admission before creating connection-owned state: a shared cap for native WebSocket and framed TCP clients, a verified-account cap within native workspaces, and a cap for the owner-only hosted workspace gateway. Count in-flight upstream handshakes as well as established connections. Release reservations on failed upgrades, timeouts, disconnect, logout and backend failure; repeated hello/login must not consume extra capacity.\n\nValidate concurrent final-slot admission, independent identities/workspaces, failed handshakes, reconnect and cleanup over real sockets and local workerd. Keep cross-workspace account quotas, edit bandwidth, aggregate RAM/storage and production compute policy open in parent 080ea85416efa648d8a634f8a1906bdecb0e70bf9da9cf934675d832d8533081. Rebuild WASM and the native session, stage the tested artifacts and restart the local session service.","files":null}]}